G4250.definition_fr:
πρίν 
   1. comme adv. de temps, avant, autrefois (cl.; 3Ma.5:28 3Mac 6:4 3Mac 6,31)
   2. Comme conic. (cl.), avant; 
   (a) après une phrase positive, avec accusatif et inf.: Mat.26:34, 75, Mrk.14:72, Luk.22:61, Jhn.4:49 8 h 58 (où D. om. γενέσθαι et π. devient prép. avec génie; voir Bl., § 69, 7) Jhn.14:29, Act.2:20" (LXX), WH, txt; πρὶν ἤ (pas si bon grenier dans cette construction; voir Bl., l.with), Mat.1:18 Mrk.14:30, Act.2:20, WH, mg., Act.7:2; 
   b) après une phrase négative, πρὶν ἤ: a. subjc. (avant ἄν, M, Pr., 169), Luk.2:26; avec optatif, Act.25:16.†
 (AS)

G4253.definition_fr:
[Passage conservé en anglais après contrôle automatique :]
πρό 
 prep. with genitive,  [in LXX chiefly for פָּנִים ;] 
before; 
 __(a) of place: Act.12:6, 14 14:13, Jas.5:9; π. προσώπου (= Heb. פָּנִים, Deu.3:18, Mal.3:1, al.; Bl., § 40, 9), Mat.11:10, Mrk.1:2, Luk.1:76 7:27 9:52 10:1, Act.14:13; 
 __(b) of time: Mat.8:29 24:38, Luk.11:38 21:12, Jhn.11:55 13:1 17:24, Act.5:36 21:38, 1Co.2:7 4:5, Eph.1:4, Col.1:17, 2Ti.1:9 4:21, Tit.1:2, Heb.11:5, 1Pe.1:20, Ju 25; π. ἐτῶν δεκατεσσάρων, fourteen years ago, 2Co.12:2; π. προσώπου (see supr.), Act.13:24; with genitive of person(s), Mat.5:12, Jhn.5:7 10:8, Rom.16:7, Gal.1:17; with genitive art. inf. (= πρίν; M, Pr., 100; Bl., § 69, 7), Mat.6:8 Luk.2:21 22:15, Jhn.1:49 13:19 17:5, Act.23:15, Gal.2:12 3:23; as in late writers (resembling a Latin idiom but indepen­dent of it; B1., § 40, 5; M, Pr., 100 f.; of. Am 2Ma.15:36, and for other exx., Soph., Lex., see word), πρὸ ἓξ ἡμέρας τοῦ πάσχα, on the sixth day before the Passover, Jhn.12:1; 
 __(with) of preference: π. πάντων, Jas.5:12, 1Pe.4:8; 
 __(d) in compos., 
 __α with subst., of position before: προαύλιον, πρόδρομος; priority of rank or order, προπάτωρ; anticipation, πρό γνωσις, πρό νοια; 
 __β with adj., intensity, πρόδηλος; 
 __γ with verb., of place, προάγω, προβαίνω; of preference, προαιρέομαι.†
 (AS)
